## Working model (Codex-specific)

- Prefer making the change, running the relevant checks, and reporting the result
  over stopping at a proposal. (Higher autonomy than the shared base implies.)

## What I use

This machine is set up via my chezmoi-managed dotfiles at
`~/Developer/personal/dotfiles`. Assume the following available; default to them
when suggesting alternatives unless a project uses something else.

- **Runtimes:** `mise` (see Environment above). Common tools for my stack:
  `java@temurin-21` / `java@temurin-25`, `gradle`, `maven`, `node`, `python`.
  New Spring Boot scaffold: `mise use java@temurin-21 gradle@latest node@lts`,
  then commit the `mise.toml`.
- **Shell / terminal:** zsh with XDG layout (`ZDOTDIR=~/.config/zsh`), `fzf`
  (`Ctrl-R`) backed by `fd`, plus `zsh-autosuggestions` / `-syntax-highlighting`
  / `-completions`. Ghostty + Zellij + Starship. `k` is aliased to `kubectl`.
- **Git & ops:** signed commits via 1Password `op-ssh-sign`; `delta` pager;
  `lazygit`; `pre-commit`.
- **Databases:** `pgcli`, `redis-cli` globally; prefer per-project datastores via
  Docker / Testcontainers over global brew services.
- **HTTP / RPC:** `httpie`, `grpcurl`, `mkcert` for local TLS.
- **Kubernetes:** `kubectl`, `k9s`, `stern`, `helm`; work-profile `kubectx` /
  `kubens`, AKS `kubelogin`, GCP `gcloud` + `gke-gcloud-auth-plugin`.
- **Cloud CLIs (work profile):** `az` (Azure), `gcloud` (GCP).
- **IaC:** Terraform (HashiCorp tap) + `tflint` + `terraform-docs`.
- **Containers:** Docker Desktop, `dive` for image introspection.

## What to suggest

- Catch correctness issues before style nits: error handling, race conditions,
  unbounded resource use, missing transaction boundaries, and missing tests for
  changed behavior.
- For installing dev CLIs globally, add them to my Brewfile rather than
  `npm install -g` / `pip install --user`.

## When working in this dotfiles repo

The repo at `~/Developer/personal/dotfiles` uses chezmoi conventions:

- Source files prefixed `dot_*` map to `~/.X`; `private_dot_*` adds mode 0600;
  `remove_*` markers delete the corresponding `~/.X`. Files ending in `.tmpl`
  are Go templates rendered with chezmoi data (name, email, signingKey, profile).
- The Brewfile is tiered: `Brewfile` (core, always) plus
  `brewfiles/Brewfile.{mac-apps,personal,work}`, layered by the brew-bundle
  script from the `profile` value and the `macApps` flag.
- Edit dotfiles via `chezmoi edit ~/.X` (editing the live `$HOME` file creates
  drift). Apply with the `chez` zsh function.
- `docs/mapping.md` is the authoritative source-to-target table — update it when
  adding/removing managed files.
